          "final_text_tail": "\nAdded a `ToolCalls.validate_input(data)` classmethod (dspy/adapters/types/tool.py:318) that normalizes varied LM output formats and returns plain Python structures (dict/list/string), not a `ToolCalls` instance:\n- **String**: parses JSON \u2014 returns the parsed dict/list if it parses to one; returns the original string unchanged if it can't be parsed.\n- **Dict with `tool_calls`**: returned as-is (existing behavior preserved).\n- **Single `{\"name\":..., \"args\":...}` dict**: wrapped into `{\"tool_calls\": [data]}`.\n- **List of tool-call dicts**: wrapped into `{\"tool_calls\": data}`.\n\n**Task 2 \u2014 Deterministic parse fingerprinting:**\n- Added `_canonicalize_args` (dspy/adapters/types/tool.py:259): recursively sorts dict keys, converts tuples\u2192lists, strips string whitespace, and preserves numeric/boolean types.\n- Added `_compute_tool_call_fingerprint` (dspy/adapters/types/tool.py:276): builds a canonical `{\"name\":..., \"args\": canonicalized_args}` object, serializes with `json.dumps(sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))`, hashes with SHA-256, returning the 64-char hex digest and its first 8 chars.\n- Added `fingerprint` and `id` fields to `ToolCalls.ToolCall`, computed once in `__init__` (dspy/adapters/types/tool.py:306). This automatically covers `from_dict_list` (which constructs `ToolCall` instances).\n\nVerified: fingerprint is deterministic across arg order, whitespace, tuple/list, and nested key order; `format()` and serialization are unaffected; all 131 adapters/primitives tests pass.",
